# Coastal Vitality

**Domain:** `https://coastalvitalitys.com/` (GoDaddy Next.js app; WordPress stays on coastalvitality.us)

## Brand & tokens

- Contact → `@/config/site`
- Logos (navbar / mobile / footer) → `@/config/brand` + `coastal-vitality-logos/`
- Fill palette CSS vars in `src/app/globals.css` (`--nv-*`)
- Locale: en

## Stack

Next.js App Router · React 19 · Tailwind v4 · Motion · Lucide · Swiper · GSAP available  
Packages rule: `.cursor/rules/packages.mdc` · UI motion/icons: `.cursor/rules/ui-controls.mdc`

## Structure

- Thin `src/app/page.tsx` (compose only)
- **Component-based:** sections in `src/components/home|layout|brand|ui|seo`
- Copy: `src/data/` · tokens: `src/config/` · helpers: `src/lib/`
- Read `src/STRUCTURE.md` + `.cursor/rules/structure-components-responsive.mdc` before large work

## Must (every UI task)

1. Correct **folder structure**
2. **Component-based** code (no page dumps)
3. **Mobile-first responsive** 320 → 1440+
4. **Icons + hover + badges + motion** (`ui-controls.mdc`)
5. Use **approved packages** only (`packages.mdc`)
6. Per-landing UI may differ (`per-landing-ui.mdc`)
7. Fast landings: follow `/think` (`fast-landing.mdc`)

## Home order

Header → Hero → (sections TBD from design) → Footer

## Per landing page (must)

- Other landings **may use completely different UI** (sections, layout, density, chrome).
- Never force Home’s structure onto another page. Follow that page’s screenshot/Figma/brief.
- Details: `.cursor/rules/per-landing-ui.mdc`

## Definition of done (UI)

1. Responsive 320 → 1440+; no horizontal scroll
2. Local media under `public/` via `@/config/brand`
3. Icons + hover + badges + `cursor-pointer`; Motion/Swiper/GSAP used as in `ui-controls` / `packages`
4. Favicon + SEO metadata + JSON-LD present
5. No em/en dashes in UI copy

## Never

- Hotlink live CDN media when local copies exist
- Hardcode brand outside config/data
- Em/en dashes in UI copy
- Commit `.env*` or `.next/`
